["",14,-17,0],["",1,-17,1],["",14,-17,1],["",30,-17,1],["",24,-9,1],["",20,-9,1],["",31,-9,1],["",32,-9,1],["",33,-9,1],["",20,-9,1],["",34,-9,1],["",35,-2,1],["",36,-2,1],["",21,-2,1],["",20,-1,1],["",1,-1,1],["",21,-1,1],["",20,0,1]],0,53],[7082144,20388,197,0.035,0.017,[[0,0.582,14,118],[1,0.418,14,79]],[],0,54],[7081132,20396,191,2.983,2.275,[[0,0.91,14,175],[1,0.09,14,16]],[["",37,-11,1],["",38,-11,1],["",39,-6,1],["",20,-6,1],["",39,-6,1],["",40,-6,1],["",37,-6,1],["",41,-6,1],["",37,-6,1]],0,54],[7129707,20402,78,1.636,1.222,[[1,15]],[],0,55],[7101742,20409,86,1.636,1.222,[[0,0.532,15,48],[1,0.468,16,38]],[["1b037537_96204ce9",42,-14,1,"We shouldn't embed magic numbers like this in the code - is there an API you can call instead to accomplish this?"],["64d42927_519254c7",14,-14,1,"Is the bug actually in `uscript_getScript`, or is `USCRIPT_INHERITED` correct??"],["f16e83fe_29a3e08d",14,-14,1,"This needs a test case"],["c45033f8_2db6c5b1",43,-11,1,"This can no longer be named `HasDefiniteScript` but rather `HasLikelyScript` or similar - as we are now introducing a heuristic behavior. This is okay with me - as this seems to be only used in…"],["e4c67231_c528a33d",44,-11,1,"I suggest to move this from `third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/win/font_fallback_win.cc` to `character.h` in a separate change."],["218018fc_b324f108",14,-10,1,"Can you add a test that includes `U+0951` not showing up as tofu anymore? That'll make sure it doesn't accidentally regress in the future."],["591b7e3a_1d68ce59",43,-7,1,"The image diffs looks like a regression, or a possible progression, I'm not sure at this point. Can you write a unit test to see how script resolutions change in the case of `U+3000` and `U+300C`…"],["5cf4c7a8_5bb35092",45,-6,0,"Can you also add the glyph from the bug (https://www.compart.com/en/unicode/U+0951)? It's always a good idea to have the exact case from the bug in your tests."],["5dd48721_9266c450",42,-6,1,"This doesn't seem to be documented anywhere, but for static methods, it's common practice to add a comment that indicates that it's static in the `.cc` file right above the definition. This is…"],["d3f661f2_becda648",45,-5,1,"Do these test pass with or without the code change in this CL? It looks like it doesn't explain why the font in Kusa-Makura and vertical-text-glyph-test were changed by this CL. Have you figure out…"],["e0921cc3_28712e30",21,-4,1,"Can you add a runtime flag as a kill-switch? Now the change is larger, we have more risks of possible regressions, and i18n feedback tend to come late, so a kill-switch should help. Sorry that I…"],["7ee980fd_a9f3c124",43,0,1,"I feel like this can be simplified further as follows: ``` bool Character::HasLikelyScript(UChar32 character) { ICUError err; UScriptCode script = uscript_getScript(character, &err); if…"],["81dd64dd_1f29bfe5",43,0,1,"I think this block fails to return `false` when the flag is off and `!U_SUCCESS(err)`. We will eventually remove the flag, so I think it's better to make the removal easy, rather than trying to share…"]],0,56],[7065396,20412,72,1.636,1.222,[[1,0.805,17,57],[0,0.195,16,15]],[["",46,-29,1],["",46,-29,1],["",3,-29,1],["470a7d47_dd507b94",47,-15,1,"Do we need an extra AtomicString - what would be the disadvantage of just keeping a boolean here that is set during initial parsing, which tells us that parsing as a valid family string failed. Then,…"],["7b3512bb_64eec8e0",48,-15,1,"I think this belongs in `css_parsing_utils`."],["ef4fd340_659a2121",11,-15,1,"I find it surprising that we would need to touch the IDL for this implementation details."],["19076f3d_a4c974c0",47,-1,1,"I think we need a bit better explanations here. Please put something in the names in how `family` and `familyName` are different. - I suggest to call this `familyNameUnquoted()`. And then please add…"],["3c252368_231bdf88",47,-1,1,"Nit: ```suggestion // rules and may require quoting names that are invalid. This is kept separate ```"],["a72b6cb9_8ec6c5d7",3,-1,1,"I would suggest to call this `SetIsInvalidFontFamilyIfNeeded` or `MaybeSetInvalidFontFamily`. Because it's not always set but only depending on the what the name looks like."]],0,57],[7162074,20412,15,0.596,0.456,[[7,3]],[],0,58],[7206314,20419,8,0.354,0.243,[[1,18]],[],0,59]]}